[
  {
    "_comment": "CAPABILITY suite for the S3 file connector (all data formats + selection modes), via `--type connectors/s3.json`. Functions in functions/caps_s3.py. `s3_out` writers (from datagen caps_input/cap_rows) write CSV/JSON/AVRO/PARQUET (+CSV format_cfg) to the `s3` bucket root; `s3_rt` readers read each back (PHASE 2 — trigger after writers commit); `s3_in` exercises glob/since/multi/none over the seeded world parquet in `s3_world_xs`. Domains: dev (datagen), s3 (round-trip write+read), s3_world_xs (seed). SRC METADATA: s3_meta_keep and s3_meta_drop (s3_in) read the same staged country parquet with and without the `tabsdata.src_metadata.drop` src_cfg key, and one transformer each in collection s3_meta (group ops) asserts that side: s3_meta_keep_check that the `@td.file.path` metadata column is there plus exactly the expected data columns, s3_meta_drop_check that no `@td.` column is left and the data columns are unchanged (functions/_srcmeta.py — which also explains why ONE transformer over both tables cannot work: an input reference puts the function in the producing plan, so it would run in each publisher's plan with the other's table missing)."
  },
  {
    "domain-manifest": {
      "domains": [
        {
          "name": "dev",
          "system": "dev"
        },
        {
          "name": "s3",
          "system": "s3"
        },
        {
          "name": "s3_world_xs",
          "system": "s3",
          "model": "world",
          "data": "xs"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "collections": [
      {
        "name": "caps_input",
        "type": "datagen_in",
        "connection_template": "connection-file:connections/datagen_in.yaml",
        "group": "sources",
        "domains": {
          "D0": "dev"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "s3_out",
        "type": "s3_file_out",
        "connection_template": "connection-file:connections/s3_file_out.yaml",
        "group": "destinations",
        "domains": {
          "D0": "s3"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "s3_rt",
        "type": "s3_file_in",
        "connection_template": "connection-file:connections/s3_file_in.yaml",
        "group": "sources",
        "domains": {
          "D0": "s3"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "s3_in",
        "type": "s3_file_in",
        "connection_template": "connection-file:connections/s3_file_in.yaml",
        "group": "sources",
        "domains": {
          "D0": "s3_world_xs"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "s3_meta",
        "type": "transform",
        "group": "ops"
      }
    ]
  },
